Q.39 Consider the following  code snippet in C language that computes the number of 
nodes in a non-empty singly linked list pointed to by the pointer variable head.  
struct node{ 
  int elt; 
  struct node *next; 
}; 
int getListSize (struct node *head) 
{ 
  if( E1 ) return 1; 
  return E2; 
} 
Which one of the following options gives the correct replacements for the 
expressions E1 and E2? 

(A) E1: head == NULL 
E2: 1 + getListSize(head) 
(B) E1: head->next == NULL 
